  "explanation": {
    "short": "å is like \"aw\" in \"saw\" (på). ø is like the vowel in \"fur\", with rounded lips (trøtt). In hj and hv the h is not said: hjemme begins like English \"y\" (YEM-meh), and hvor and hva begin with a \"v\" (VOOR, VAH).",
    "more": "æ, ø and å are letters of their own at the end of the alphabet, not a, o or e with a mark. Writing them correctly is part of spelling: å is not the same letter as a."
  },
